

# Report invalid search queries passed to the search API

* assigned: alex, arun
* tags: enhancement

* status: in progress



genenetwork2 offloads search to the genenetwork3 search API. When there is an error in the genenetwork3 API call, genenetwork2 has no idea what went wrong and cannot produce a good stacktrace. The genenetwork3 API should do a better job of communicating errors.

In particular, for the search API, we should start with correctly reporting invalid search queries so that genenetwork2 can present it appropriately in its web UI.

## Update: 2026-10-06

Two developments on the gn4 path (gn4 now fronts search at
/search with its own envelope and authorization):

* The reporting half is in place there: gn4 maps gn3's 400 parser
  errors to a 422 `invalid_query` response carrying gn3's actual
  diagnostic, so a caller always sees a structured error instead of
  silence (merged to gn4 main 2026-10-05, with an offline contract
  mirror in test/python/test_search.py).
* The definition of "invalid" moved underneath us, though:
  production /api3/search no longer rejects some malformed queries.
  Verified 2026-10-06, the inputs "a&&b", "alcohol &&" and
  "position:" now return 200 with up to 100 hits -- the query is
  sanitized before parsing ("a&&b" returns the exact match set of
  "a b"; "position:" of "position"). The 400 diagnostics that
  gn4's frozen tests recorded on 2026-10-03/04 reflect the older
  behavior. Which behavior is authoritative is an open question
  with Pjotr: deliberate sanitize-and-search, or a regression of
  the strict parse.

The native-search migration notes carry the surrounding context:

=> ../topics/gn4/gn4-search-native.gmi search native migration

The gn2/gn3-facing half of this issue (gn3 communicating errors to
  gn2's web UI) remains open as originally written.

Update 2026-10-08: the structured-invalid-query contract is settled for
gn4. Agreed 2026-10-06: every malformed query that reaches parsing is
answered with a 422 `invalid_query` body —

    {"error": {"type": "invalid_query", "message": "...",
               "param": "query",
               "detail": {"xapian_error_type": "..."}}}

— carrying the underlying diagnostic, on top of the 400-mapping already
in gn4 main. The gn4 native search engine implements the full contract
(2026-10-07, native-search-engine branch): parser rejections, invalid
numeric-range values, and invalid position/Hs/Mm fields all return the
typed 422 instead of a 200-empty or a 500. The earlier open question —
whether /api3's sanitize-and-search behavior is authoritative — remains
open with the gn3 owner. This closes the gn4 half of the issue; the
gn2/gn3 UI-facing half remains as originally written.
